    // = P(u <= x)P(v >= x) + P(v <= x)P(u >= x)
    // = (x/l)((l-x)/l) + ((l-x)/l)(x/l)
    // = 2x(l-x)/l^2
    //
    // For n independent segments, the number of segments covering x follows a binomial distribution
    // with parameters n and p(x) = 2x(l-x)/l^2.
    //
    // The expected total length is the integral over x of P(at least k segments cover x) * dx.
    // E = ∫_0^l P(Bin(n, p(x)) >= k) dx
    //
    // P(Bin(n, p) >= k) = sum_{i=k}^{n} C(n, i) p^i (1-p)^{n-i}
    //
