    // The 2n endpoints split [0, l] into 2n+1 intervals. Let the endpoints be sorted:
    // 0 = t_0 <= t_1 <= ... <= t_{2n} = l (but actually the endpoints are random, so we don't know their values)
    //
    // Actually, a better approach: Consider each infinitesimal interval dx at position x.
    // The contribution to the expected length is P(at least k segments cover x) dx.
    // So E = ∫_0^l P(at least k segments cover x) dx.
    //
    // Let's compute this integral.
    // p(x) = 2x(l-x)/l^2
    //
